# Shared preamble, included by every stage template in this
# directory via Jinja's `include` directive (scripts/render_template.py's
# Jinja Environment uses a
# FileSystemLoader rooted at this directory, so includes resolve between
# sibling template files with no extra plumbing). Added 2026-11-08 when
# step 2 chis stages 4-5 moved from one continuous LAMMPS session into
# separate Snakemake rules -- see rules/step2_equilibrate.smk's module
# docstring for why that split is now safe (merged_coeffs.lmp carries
# bond/angle/dihedral_coeff commands explicitly, so write_data no longer
# needs to preserve `bond_style hybrid harmonic`'s Coeffs sections across
# stages).
#
# `params.read_data` is the one thing that varies per stage (each stage
# reads the previous stage's write_data output, except the first, which
# reads merged.data itself); every other setting here is identical for
# every stage.
units real
atom_style full
boundary p p p

bond_style hybrid harmonic
angle_style hybrid harmonic
dihedral_style hybrid multi/harmonic
special_bonds lj 0.0 0.0 0.5 coul 0.0 0.0 0.5
pair_style lj/cut/coul/long {{ params.cutoff }}
kspace_style pppm {{ params.kspace_accuracy }}

# pair_style must be declared before read_data -- confirmed live
# 2026-11-08: unlike merge_slab.py's merged.data (which deliberately has
# no "Pair Coeffs" section at all, see its own module docstring), a
# write_data checkpoint from any LAMMPS stage below DOES embed one for
# this plain (non-hybrid) pair_style, and read_data errors ("Must define
# pair_style before Pair Coeffs") if pair_style isn't already known. The
# embedded values get overwritten by merged_coeffs.lmp's pair_coeff
# commands below regardless, so this doesn't depend on what read_data
# happened to load from that section.
read_data {{ params.read_data }}

include merged_coeffs.lmp
pair_modify mix geometric

group mobile type 1:{{ params.n_org_types }}
group substrate type {{ params.n_org_types + 1 }}:{{ params.n_org_types + 2 }}
velocity substrate set 0.0 0.0 0.0

# Stage 5's density profiles need the single adsorbing fragment split out
# from the many hexadecane molecules within `mobile`. Confirmed live
# 2026-11-06 for both ST and MMA (unwrapped.gro / converted.lmp): a
# fragment_length=1 "CH3-{species}-CH3" capped repeat unit is written by
# GROMACS/polyply as THREE separate molecule-IDs (cap, core, cap --
# residues "1CH3"/"2{species}"/"3CH3" in the .gro), always 1-3 since the
# fragment is always the very first molecule in topol.top's [molecules]
# section (see rules/step2_dilute.smk). Hexadecane molecule-IDs start
# right after at 4 and run up to merge_slab.py's max_org_molid (passed in
# below; the substrate itself gets the one molid right after that, not
# needed here since it's already selected by atom type above).
group fragment molecule 1:3
group hexadecane molecule 4:{{ params.max_org_molid }}

neighbor 2.0 bin
neigh_modify every 1 delay 0 check yes

compute mobtemp mobile temp
# `compute pressure` requires group "all" (the virial is inherently a
# global per-box quantity, confirmed live 2026-11-08 -- "Compute pressure
# must use group all") -- only the temperature-compute argument used for
# its kinetic term is group-scoped.
compute mobpress all pressure mobtemp

timestep {{ params.timestep_fs }}
